# Frontend Architecture

## Layout

```
edge-fe/src/
  components/     # App shell (layout/) + shadcn UI (ui/) + shared (common/)
  features/<name>/  # Domain slices
  lib/            # axios, cn(), shared utilities
  providers/      # Theme, Query, AppProviders
  router/         # Lazy routes
  i18n/           # en + sr translations
```

## Feature slice structure

Each feature under `features/<name>/` should contain only what it needs:

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `pages/` | Route-level components |
| `components/` | Feature UI |
| `api/` | Data access (axios or mock store) |
| `hooks/` | React Query wrappers |
| `store/` | Zustand mock/client state |
| `schemas/` | Zod factories with i18n |
| `types/` | Entities + request DTOs |
| `lib/` | Pure helpers (DnD, drafts) |

Cross-cutting UI without its own routes lives in `features/content/` (consumed by screens + playlists).

## Import alias

Use `@/` for all imports from `src/` (e.g. `@/features/auth/api/authApi`).

## Adding a feature

1. Create slice folders under `features/<name>/`
2. Add lazy page import in `router/index.tsx`
3. Add nav item in `AppSidebarNav.tsx` if needed
4. Add i18n keys in both `en` and `sr` translation files
5. Wire `api/*.ts` to axios when backend exists; use mock store pattern until then (see `state-and-api.mdc`)
